# Generic Maker-Checker Data Management App — Design

Nov 2, 2026 · Ameya Kalamkar

## Overview

A generic, config-driven web app (React + Spring Boot REST) to browse and change Oracle tables under maker-checker control, with SCD2-style in-table lineage and data-level entitlement enforced in the DAO. Other SQL databases are supported later through a dialect layer.

**In scope**

- Read-only browsing of entitled data, grouped by business domain
- Record-level create, update and delete through maker-checker approval
- Bulk CSV upload per table, validated asynchronously, approved as one request
- Full lineage per business record (Z record) plus a workflow audit trail
- Every operation has a generic default and can be overridden with Spring beans

**Design principles**

- Configuration in code (versioned JSON in git), not in framework tables
- Pending changes never touch business tables until approved
- Entitlement fails closed; no code path reaches a table without it
- Identifiers come only from validated metadata; all values are bind parameters

